diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ada4c02..b7719c0 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -51,6 +51,12 @@ The status pill first confirms Decaid availability and then the machine device's
 
 The header Sleep control sends `sleeping` and shows the clock at the configured screensaver brightness (7% by default). Settings → Power → Screen brightness → Screen off after optionally blacks out the screen after a delay; 0 disables this. A single tap on the black screen restores the clock at screensaver brightness and restarts the delay without waking the machine. A one-second hold on either the clock or black screen wakes the machine and restores normal screen brightness. Taps while the clock is visible do not extend the delay. The Settings control opens Decaid's bundled settings interface with `backName=Bestpresso` so its Back control returns to the skin.
 
+## Shot analysis and dial-in
+
+After a pull, and on any saved shot in Insights, **Dial in** opens a display-only sheet. It shows what the puck did, using Decent's resistance convention (pressure ÷ flow²): possible channels (abrupt relative resistance drops that the profile didn't command, ignoring stage changes and the final two seconds), stalled flow at high pressure, time to first drops, and the shape of the puck's breakdown. Findings are also marked on the chart. A 3 × 3 espresso compass (sour ↔ bitter, weak ↔ strong) plus a drying-finish flag produces **one** next step from the shot's real dose, yield and grind. Puck problems come first, and yield is adjusted before grind. Taste notes stay on the tablet, keyed per gateway and shot. Nothing is written to Decaid and no machine setting changes. The **Calm** control on the live screen swaps the chart for a single yield ring while the shot runs, and the choice is remembered.
+
+Thresholds are not yet calibrated against real shots. Run `node --experimental-strip-types scripts/analyze-shots.ts --gateway YOUR_DECAID_IP --limit 100 --csv shots.csv` to compare findings with shots you remember. Rules, references and the calibration bar are in [docs/shot-analysis-and-dial-in.md](docs/shot-analysis-and-dial-in.md). Review it with sample data at `/review/dial-in/index.html` in development.
+
